  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Peter Bull was preparing to take his luxury charter business to the Mediterranean when a former schoolmate encountered him on the Hamble in 1972. Bull invited the visiting crew aboard to see his latest acquisition. Its elaborate interior was intended to appeal to the celebrity clients he hoped to attract.\n\nWith Pauline Bull, he took direct responsibility for a major conversion project. From a facility in Poole, the couple hired around fifty craftsmen, designers and naval architects. They coordinated several years of work before the new charter service began operating in 2005.",
